# What the glmark2 image runs (driver/docs/glmark2.md).

menu "glmark2"

config GLMARK2_SIZE
	string "Window size, WxH"
	default "800x600"
	help
	  The size of the board window, handed to glmark2 as --size. 800x600
	  is glmark2's own default (options.cpp:37) and the size of most
	  published glmark2-es2 runs on these boards; it fits all three panels
	  (1024x600, 1280x800, 1920x720). A window larger than the board can
	  give is refused by board_window() at the start of the run.

config GLMARK2_ARGS
	string "More glmark2 arguments, separated by spaces"
	default ""
	help
	  Appended after --size, e.g. "--off-screen" or
	  "-b build:use-vbo=true -b texture". Empty: the default benchmark
	  list (default-benchmarks.h, 33 scenes of 10 s each). --size and
	  --fullscreen here are refused (the window is sized from
	  GLMARK2_SIZE); --results-file needs a file system and is refused.

config GLMARK2_PVR_ONE_KICK_IN_FLIGHT
	bool "PowerVR: one kick in flight (measurement)"
	depends on YAKOGL_DRV_GPU_PVR
	help
	  Sets the PowerVR backend's PVR_BACKEND_OPT_ONE_IN_FLIGHT before the
	  first scene: each swap waits for its own frame's kick, not only for
	  the ones before it, so every kick starts on an idle GPU. With
	  CONFIG_YAKOGL_DRV_GPU_PVR_KICK_TIMES the kick line then shows the alone
	  cost of a frame's kick
	  (docs/notes/pvr-fence-wait.md, "The next
	  experiment"). A measurement knob: off for a score.

config GLMARK2_FRAME_DUMP
	bool "Print each scene's last frame as text on the console"
	help
	  After a scene's last frame is read back for the picture value, prints
	  the whole window as "glmark2-fb:" lines (one base64 RGB888 row per
	  line, with the row number and a crc16, then a crc32 of the frame):
	  800x600 is about 1.9 MB, minutes of UART. tools/cts/glmark2-fb.py
	  turns the console log into a PNG (driver/docs/glmark2.md, "The frame
	  dump"). For a picture of one scene (GLMARK2_ARGS names it); off in every
	  gate and common-set image.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
